  },
  "locales": {
    "en": {
      "title": "The gerund",
      "summary": "The gerund is the -ing form used as a noun.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "The gerund is the -ing form of a verb used as a noun."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Swimming** is fun.",
                "I enjoy **reading**.",
                "She is good at **cooking**."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "A gerund can be a subject, an object or the object of a preposition. It is the form used after prepositions: after leaving, before eating, instead of waiting."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>subject</td><td><strong>Walking is healthy.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>object</td><td><strong>I like dancing.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>after a preposition</td><td><strong>He left without saying goodbye.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
